// Tree positions for the Blacks sim, extracted from real USGS lidar canopy.
// Source: USGS 3DEP lidar point cloud CA_SanDiegoQL2_2014 (EPT, usgs-lidar-public
// on AWS), same 2014 San Diego survey as the bare-earth terrain. Method: canopy
// height model (first-return/veg-class height above ground-class returns, 1.5 m
// cells) -> 5x5 local maxima >= 2.5 m -> building rejection (plateau area > 70 m^2
// with no ground visibility) -> cliff-edge artifact rejection (ground relief within
// 4 m > max(3 m, 0.8h)). z_ground sampled from data/terrain.js heightfield inside
// the sim domain (matches the render mesh), lidar ground grid outside. 2026-07-11.
// Local frame: x east / y north / z up, meters; origin = sim domain SW corner.
// Covers x in [0,2400], y in [-60,4700] (extends ~2.7 km north into Torrey Pines
// State Reserve beyond the sim domain). Trees sorted by y (south first).
window.BLACKS_TREES = {
  count: 14050,
  stride: 5,  // x, y, z_ground, height, radius (Float32, base64)
  b64: "",
  notes: "14050 trees total, 6372 inside the 2400x2021 sim domain. Heights 2.5-43 m (median ~9 m: coastal scrub + Torrey pines; tall = eucalyptus at UCSD SE corner). radius = crown radius est. from CHM area, clamped to 0.3-0.7x height. Vintage 2014; on-campus construction since then not reflected."
};
